# deploy.env.example — template for scripts/deploy.env (gitignored, operator-local).
# Copy this file to scripts/deploy.env, then uncomment and fill in each line below.
# Every assignment here stays commented: a copied-but-unedited file leaves the scripts
# on their existing exit-2 "missing configuration" path instead of sending a
# placeholder value to ssh or an HTTP client.
# Format: the scripts read this file as KEY=value data and never execute it. Quotes
# (double or single) are optional, the contents are taken literally (`$` is not
# expanded), and any line other than a blank line, a comment or a KEY=value line for
# one of the three keys below is refused.

# The ssh alias deploy.sh reaches the deployment host through. An alias, so no host
# name needs to appear anywhere in this file or in the repository.
#FORQSITE_HELP_DEPLOY_HOST="REPLACE_ME_WITH_SSH_ALIAS"

# The per-site directory on the far side of that alias that deploy.sh writes the two
# bundles and the provenance sidecar into.
#FORQSITE_HELP_DEPLOY_DIR="REPLACE_ME_WITH_REMOTE_DIR"

# The base URL drift-check.sh fetches the served bundle bytes from. No trailing slash.
#FORQSITE_HELP_SITE_URL="REPLACE_ME_WITH_SITE_URL"
